<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02GY">Example <span data-tag="02GY">5.2.8.13</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ denote its homotopy category, which we regard as enriched over the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ of Kan complexes. Applying Proposition <a data-tag="02GT" href="/tag/02GT">5.2.8.7</a>, we obtain the following: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
For every object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the corepresentable $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$-enriched functor 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}} \quad \quad D \mapsto \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(C,D) \]
</div>
<p>
 is the enriched homotopy transport representation for the left fibration $\{ C\}  \vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For every object $D \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the representable $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$-enriched functor 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}} \quad \quad C \mapsto \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(C,D) \]
</div>
<p>
 is the enriched homotopy transport representation for the right fibration $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \{ D\}  \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
